### React Component Usage

Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons/blob/main/README.md

Import and configure icon components using the @tabler/icons-react package.

```jsx
import { IconAward } from '@tabler/icons-react';

const MyComponent = () => {
  return <IconAward
    size={36} // set custom `width` and `height`
    color="red" // set `stroke` color
    stroke={3}  // set `stroke-width`
    strokeLinejoin="miter" // override other SVG props
  />
}
```

--------------------------------

### Icon Component Usage

Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons/blob/main/docs/icons/react.mdx

How to import and render an icon component in a React application with custom properties.

```APIDOC
## Icon Component

### Description
Each icon is a tree-shakable React component that can be imported directly from the package. Props can be passed to customize the appearance of the icon.

### Props
- **size** (Number) - Optional - The width and height of the icon in pixels. Default: 24.
- **color** (String) - Optional - The stroke color of the icon. Default: currentColor.
- **stroke** (Number) - Optional - The stroke width of the icon. Default: 2.

### Usage Example
```jsx
import { IconArrowLeft } from '@tabler/icons-react';

const App = () => {
  return <IconArrowLeft color="red" size={48} stroke={2} />;
};
```
```

--------------------------------

### IconProps type includes stroke as optional override

Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons/blob/main/packages/icons-react/src/types.ts

The `IconProps` interface extends standard SVG props and exposes `stroke` as an optional `string | number`. No global or provider-based mechanism exists in the package.

```typescript
export interface IconProps extends Partial<Omit<React.ComponentPropsWithoutRef<'svg'>, 'stroke'>> {
  size?: string | number;
  stroke?: string | number;
  title?: string;
}

export type Icon = FunctionComponent<IconProps>;

export type TablerIcon = ForwardRefExoticComponent<IconProps & RefAttributes<SVGSVGElement>>;
```

--------------------------------

### Per-icon stroke default via createReactComponent

Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons/blob/main/packages/icons-react/src/createReactComponent.ts

Each icon component assigns `stroke` a hardcoded default of `2` in its destructured props. There is no React context, global configuration, or provider — stroke must be set per-instance or via a custom wrapper.

```typescript
const Component = forwardRef<SVGSVGElement, IconProps>(
  (
    { color = 'currentColor', size = 24, stroke = 2, title, className, children, ...rest }: IconProps,
    ref,
  ) =>
    createElement(
      'svg',
      {
        ref,
        ...defaultAttributes[type],
        width: size,
        height: size,
        className: [`tabler-icon`, `tabler-icon-${iconName}`, className].join(' '),
        ...(type === 'filled'
          ? {
              fill: color,
            }
          : {
              strokeWidth: stroke,
              stroke: color,
            }),
        ...rest,
      },
      [
        title && createElement('title', { key: 'svg-title' }, title),
        ...iconNode.map(([tag, attrs]) => createElement(tag, attrs)),
        ...(Array.isArray(children) ? children : [children]),
      ],
    ),
);
```

### Tabler Icons for React > How to use > Props

Source: https://github.com/tabler/tabler-icons/blob/main/docs/icons/react.mdx

Icons support customization through standard props. You can adjust the icon size, color, and stroke width to fit your design requirements. The default size is 24, the default color is currentColor, and the default stroke width is 2.

